A NOTE ON WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO
----------------------------------------
This file is a statement of terms, not a lock. It cannot stop anyone from
downloading the code — nothing can, because a browser has to be given the code
in order to run it. What it does is remove the defence of "there was no licence,
so I assumed it was free to take". Without this file, a public repository is
widely *treated* as fair game even though copyright still applies by default;
with it, the terms are explicit and on the record, dated, and in version
control.

That is the whole of the realistic protection available to a client-side web
application, and it is worth more than obfuscation, which delays a determined
reader by minutes and costs you debuggability forever.

While the repository at github.com/KaonHew02/FinSim remains public, GitHub's own
Terms of Service additionally allow any GitHub user to view and fork it within
GitHub. Making the repository private is the only way to withdraw that, and it
is a separate decision with consequences for hosting — see BUILD.md.
